📅 Day 29 – Java Integration with MySQL Database

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on integrating Java applications with the MySQL database using JDBC. The mentor explained how Java programs establish a connection with a MySQL database to perform various data operations.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to MySQL Connectivity

Java applications interact with databases using JDBC drivers.

MySQL is a widely used relational database management system (RDBMS).

JDBC enables communication between Java programs and MySQL databases.

2️⃣ Steps for Java–MySQL Connection

The mentor demonstrated the steps involved in connecting Java with MySQL:

Load the JDBC driver

Establish connection using DriverManager

Create a Statement or PreparedStatement

Execute SQL queries

Retrieve results using ResultSet

Close the database connection

3️⃣ JDBC Components Used

DriverManager → Manages database drivers and establishes connection

Connection → Represents connection with database

Statement / PreparedStatement → Executes SQL queries

ResultSet → Retrieves data returned by SQL queries

🔹 Practical Implementation

During the practice session, I implemented sample programs to:

Connect a Java application with a MySQL database

Insert records into database tables

Retrieve stored data using SQL queries

Display database results using Java programs

This helped me understand how backend applications interact with databases in real-world systems.